  description: "A graduate-level continuing education course preparing licensed mental health clinicians to address sexual health within the lives of clients living with chronic illness and disability. Grounded in the World Health Organization's International Classification of Functioning, Disability and Health (ICF) and a disability-affirming, biopsychosocial framework, this course examines condition-specific impacts on sexual function and intimacy across cardiovascular disease, diabetes, cancer, multiple sclerosis, spinal cord injury, and chronic pain. Clinicians will build skills in assessment, psychoeducation, scope-appropriate intervention, and interprofessional collaboration.",
